;ignorehitpause =
;persistent =

;The math equation for this parabola is:

;-C / ((((B - 150) - (A + (B - 150)) / 2) ^ 2) / ((B - 150) - A)) * (((x - (A + (B - 150)) / 2) ^ 2) / ((B - 150) - A)) + C = 0 AND y >= 0

;A = Your stage default starting point

;B = Your opponent's stage starting point

;C = Height of parabola

;This equation will create a parabola no matter where A is (as long as it is less than B - 150) and no matter where B is

;NOTE there might be a slight bit of error from gravity.

;OR The parabola might actually be a half circle, I'm not sure

;The equation of the half circle is:

;(C / ((B - 150) - (A + (B - 150)) / 2))((((B - 150) - (A + (B - 150)) / 2) ^ 2) - ((x - (A + (B - 150)) / 2) ^ 2)) ^ .5 = 0

;A = Your stage default starting point

;B = Your opponent's stage starting point

;C = Height of half circle

